## Overview

FirstLook helps game studios understand and engage their players. Its dashboard brings together what players say on Discord, what they do in the game, and how they answer surveys, so a team can see how a game is being received and act on it.

This project collects the work that shaped the dashboard around how teams actually operate: thinking in events rather than dates, managing many games at once, and getting help without leaving the page they're on.

## Custom events in date filters

*November 2025*

Teams think about time in terms of playtests, launches, and betas, not calendar dates. The date picker now lets them save a range as a named custom event under My Events, using the "+" beside it. Saved events work as one-click filters in Sentiment and Creator Content, next to the usual suggested ranges.

## Publisher organizations

*March 2026*

Publishers manage several studios and games at once, which the single-game dashboard wasn't built for. Publisher organizations add a dedicated overview with total active players across every game, per-studio permissions, and a games list where publishers can mark games active or inactive for billing.

## Agent on every page

*September 2026*

The Agent was already a page of its own. It now appears on most pages of the dashboard through a control at the bottom of the layout, which opens a chat panel over whatever the person is looking at.

The panel is labeled "Focus on" the page they came from, so they can ask about a column, a spike, or what to do next without explaining where they are. It uses the same player data, confirmations, and actions as the full Agent page, can be expanded for more room, and can open the full page for chat history and skills. Cmd/Ctrl + K and `/ask` still launch it.
